 "result": "The failing call is at `src/tessel/sessions.py:374`, in `SignedCookieSessionInterface.persist_session`:\n\n```python\nresponse.set_cookie(\n    name,\n    val,\n    expires=expires,\n    httponly=httponly,\n    domain=domain,\n    path=path,\n    secure=secure,\n    partitioned=partitioned,\n    samesite=samesite,\n)\n```\n\nThe installed Werkzeug 3.0.3 rejects the **`partitioned`** keyword argument (`partitioned=partitioned`), raising `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`.\n\nLine 374 is where the `response.set_cookie(` call starts, and the traceback anchors there. The value comes from `self.get_cookie_partitioned(app)`, a few lines above in the same method. The `response.delete_cookie(...)` branch in the same method also passes `partitioned=partitioned`. It would fail the same way, but no test I ran reached it.",
